From 883bbc62b60a6e230fef0ec192a3ef49214af297 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marks-jhojan <153632015+marks-jhojan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:31:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] runtime: UNDS control channel: adaptive triggers and
 light bar through SDL

The companion no longer writes the DualSense itself (hidapi, USB only, a
second writer of the output report next to SDL). It answers to the
address the UNDS events come from with 37-byte binary datagrams and the
runtime hands them to SDL_SendGamepadEffect, so SDL's HIDAPI PS5 driver
stays the only writer, over USB and Bluetooth alike:

  0 "UNDC"  4 version 1  5 flags (1 R2, 2 L2, 4 light bar, 8 release)
  8 seq (u32 LE)  12 R2 effect (11 bytes)  23 L2 effect  34 r g b

- On with UNDS_EVENTS unless UNDS_FX=0. The event socket is bound before
  its first send (to 127.0.0.1 for a loopback companion) and only takes
  datagrams from the UNDS_EVENTS host; SIO_UDP_CONNRESET is turned off on
  Windows so a hello sent while nobody listens does not break recvfrom.
- The event socket is overlapped on Windows (what socket() gives): a
  synchronous WSASocketW handle serializes every operation, and each
  sendto from the game's and the audio threads waited for the fx
  receiver's select (6.27 s for three pad events in unds-test; 160 us
  after the change).
- A receiver thread (select, 100 ms) writes each command at once; SDL
  queues it for its rumble thread (no wait in the game's threads). Only
  the trigger and light bar enable bits are ever set, never rumble
  emulation (which turns the audio haptics off); trigger modes outside
  the controller's known set are rejected.
- While the companion holds the light bar, scePadSetLightBar is still
  published but not shown; on release (command, 5 s without datagrams,
  or bye) both triggers go off and the game's colour comes back. At bye
  the release gets 30 ms to reach the controller before the process
  exits. After a controller reconnects the held state is written again.
- Every command gets an "fx" event (ok, time to SDL); hello gains fx,
  fxp, fxc, fxr, fxe, fxo; the exit report gains an fx line.
- runtime_pad.c: runtime_pad_unds_effect (DualSense only: other pads are
  logged once and ignored), runtime_pad_unds_generation and
  runtime_pad_unds_game_led.
- unds-test covers the channel against a stand-in of runtime_pad.c:
  report layout, rejections, keep-alive, reconnect, release, watchdog,
  bye. It accepts datagrams reordered between sender threads (each seq
  must still arrive exactly once), measures the pad rate-limit calls
  instead of assuming they fit in 8 ms, uses a 4 KiB receive buffer
  (Windows refuses longer datagrams), prints the last datagram on a
  failed assertion and fails if a sendto takes 250 ms or more.
  UNDS_VERSION 0.5.0, protocol stays 1 (fields and one event added).

Tested on Windows 11 (unds-test; in game hundreds of commands, 0
rejected, 0 SDL failures, triggers released on the companion's Ctrl+C,
Alt+F4 and the window's X) and under Wine.

Without UNDS_EVENTS nothing changes and nothing is printed.

